---
import { site } from "@lukebrannagan/content";
import PageLayout from "../layouts/PageLayout.astro";

const updated = "6 September 2026";
---

<PageLayout title="Accessibility" description={site.accessibility.lede}>
	<ds-container>
		<article class="statement">
			<ds-stack gap="xl">
				<header>
					<ds-stack gap="sm">
						<ds-breadcrumb
							items={JSON.stringify([
								{ label: "Home", href: "/" },
								{ label: "Accessibility" },
							])}
						></ds-breadcrumb>
						<ds-text as="h1" variant="display">Accessibility</ds-text>
						<ds-text variant="muted">
							{site.accessibility.lede} Last reviewed {updated}.
						</ds-text>
					</ds-stack>
				</header>

				<section aria-labelledby="aim-heading">
					<ds-stack gap="sm">
						<ds-text as="h2" id="aim-heading" variant="meta">Aim</ds-text>
						<p>
							I build this site to work with keyboard, screen readers, and
							{" "}
							<code>prefers-reduced-motion</code>
							. The target is
							{" "}
							<ds-link href="https://www.w3.org/TR/WCAG22/" external>
								WCAG 2.2 Level AA
							</ds-link>
							. I have not commissioned a formal audit, so this is not a claim of full
							conformance.
						</p>
					</ds-stack>
				</section>

				<section aria-labelledby="works-heading">
					<ds-stack gap="sm">
						<ds-text as="h2" id="works-heading" variant="meta">What is in place</ds-text>
						<ul class="statement__list">
							<li>
								Skip links to main content and primary nav on every page.
							</li>
							<li>
								Visible focus styles on interactive controls; hit targets sized for
								pointer and keyboard use.
							</li>
							<li>
								Native buttons, links, checkboxes, and search fields for filters and
								chrome. Pressed topic and series chips use
								{" "}
								<code>aria-pressed</code>
								.
							</li>
							<li>
								Writing filter results announce count changes in a polite live region.
							</li>
							<li>
								Motion (card lift, page enter, bookshelf hover) respects
								{" "}
								<code>prefers-reduced-motion</code>
								.
							</li>
							<li>
								Storybook includes the a11y addon for design-system and site shell
								stories.
							</li>
						</ul>
					</ds-stack>
				</section>

				<section aria-labelledby="gaps-heading">
					<ds-stack gap="sm">
						<ds-text as="h2" id="gaps-heading" variant="meta">Known limits</ds-text>
						<ul class="statement__list">
							<li>
								When the book-reviews shelf is published on wide viewports, it uses a
								Three.js canvas. The canvas is decorative for assistive tech; a visually
								hidden link list carries the same destinations. Narrow viewports use a
								plain list instead. Hover-to-pull interaction is mouse-oriented.
							</li>
							<li>
								Individual book pages can show a 3D cover viewer. Title, author, rating,
								and the review text remain available without that viewer.
							</li>
							<li>
								Some older writing was imported from elsewhere. Structure and alt text
								may be thinner on those posts than on newer ones.
							</li>
							<li>
								Third-party destinations (GitHub, LinkedIn, Amazon affiliate links) follow
								their own accessibility practices, not mine.
							</li>
						</ul>
					</ds-stack>
				</section>

				<section aria-labelledby="test-heading">
					<ds-stack gap="sm">
						<ds-text as="h2" id="test-heading" variant="meta">How I check</ds-text>
						<p>
							Keyboard passes on new pages and filters. Spot checks with VoiceOver on
							macOS. Automated checks in Storybook and during local builds. That is a
							maintenance habit, not a full WCAG evaluation.
						</p>
					</ds-stack>
				</section>

				<section aria-labelledby="report-heading">
					<ds-stack gap="sm">
						<ds-text as="h2" id="report-heading" variant="meta">Tell me what breaks</ds-text>
						<p>
							If something is hard to use, email
							{" "}
							<ds-link href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</ds-link>
							. Include the page URL, what you were trying to do, and the browser or
							assistive tech if you know it. I will reply and fix what I can.
						</p>
					</ds-stack>
				</section>
			</ds-stack>
		</article>
	</ds-container>
</PageLayout>

<style>
	.statement {
		max-width: var(--measure);
	}

	.statement p {
		margin: 0;
		font-size: var(--font-size-md);
		line-height: var(--line-height-relaxed);
		color: var(--color-fg);
	}

	.statement__list {
		margin: 0;
		padding-inline-start: 1.25rem;
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: var(--space-sm);
		font-size: var(--font-size-md);
		line-height: var(--line-height-relaxed);
		color: var(--color-fg);
	}

	.statement code {
		font-family: var(--font-mono);
		font-size: 0.92em;
	}
</style>
